
[1mSynopsis[22m

  $ quicktype [[1m--lang[22m LANG] [[1m--src-lang[22m SRC_LANG] [[1m--out[22m FILE] FILE|URL ...     
                                                                                
  LANG ... cjson|c++|cr|cs|dart|elixir|elm|flow|go|haskell|java|js|javascript-  
  prop-                                                                         
  types|schema|kotlin|objc|php|pike|py|ruby|rs|scala3|smithy4a|swift|ts|typescript- 
  effect-schema|typescript-zod                                                  
                                                                                
  SRC_LANG ... json|schema|graphql|postman|typescript                           

[1mDescription[22m

  Given JSON sample data, quicktype outputs code for working with that data in  
  C (cJSON), C++, Crystal, C#, Dart, Elixir, Elm, Flow, Go, Haskell, Java,      
  JavaScript, JavaScript PropTypes, JSON Schema, Kotlin, Objective-C, PHP,      
  Pike, Python, Ruby, Rust, Scala3, Smithy, Swift, TypeScript, TypeScript       
  Effect Schema, TypeScript Zod.                                                

[1mOptions[22m

 [1m-o[22m, [1m--out[22m FILE                                              The output file. Determines --lang and --top-level.        
 [1m-t[22m, [1m--top-level[22m NAME                                        The name for the top level type.                           
 [1m-l[22m, [1m--lang[22m LANG                                             The target language.                                       
 [1m-s[22m, [1m--src-lang[22m SRC_LANG                                     The source language (default is json).                     
 [1m--src[22m FILE|URL|DIRECTORY                                    The file, url, or data directory to type.                  
 [1m--src-urls[22m FILE                                             Tracery grammar describing URLs to crawl.                  
 [1m--no-maps[22m                                                   Don't infer maps, always use classes.                      
 [1m--no-enums[22m                                                  Don't infer enums, always use strings.                     
 [1m--no-uuids[22m                                                  Don't convert UUIDs to UUID objects.                       
 [1m--no-date-times[22m                                             Don't infer dates or times.                                
 [1m--no-integer-strings[22m                                        Don't convert stringified integers to integers.            
 [1m--no-boolean-strings[22m                                        Don't convert stringified booleans to booleans.            
 [1m--no-combine-classes[22m                                        Don't combine similar classes.                             
 [1m--no-ignore-json-refs[22m                                       Treat $ref as a reference in JSON.                         
 [1m--graphql-schema[22m FILE                                       GraphQL introspection file.                                
 [1m--graphql-introspect[22m URL                                    Introspect GraphQL schema from a server.                   
 [1m--http-method[22m METHOD                                        HTTP method to use for the GraphQL introspection query.    
 [1m--http-header[22m HEADER                                        Header(s) to attach to all HTTP requests, including the    
                                                             GraphQL introspection query.                               
 [1m-S[22m, [1m--additional-schema[22m FILE                                Register the $id's of additional JSON Schema files.        
 [1m--alphabetize-properties[22m                                    Alphabetize order of class properties.                     
 [1m--all-properties-optional[22m                                   Make all class properties optional.                        
 [1m--quiet[22m                                                     Don't show issues in the generated code.                   
 [1m--debug[22m OPTIONS or all                                      Comma separated debug options: print-graph, print-         
                                                             reconstitution, print-gather-names, print-transformations, 
                                                             print-schema-resolving, print-times, provenance            
 [1m--telemetry[22m enable|disable                                  Enable anonymous telemetry to help improve quicktype       
 [1m-h[22m, [1m--help[22m                                                  Get some help.                                             
 [1m-v[22m, [1m--version[22m                                               Display the version of quicktype                           

[1mOptions for C (cJSON)[22m

 [1m--source-style[22m single-source|multi-source                   Source code generation type, whether to generate single or 
                                                             multiple source files                                      
 [1m--integer-size[22m int8_t|int16_t|int32_t|int64_t               Integer code generation type (int64_t by default)          
 [1m--hashtable-size[22m SIZE                                       Hashtable size, used when maps are created (64 by default) 
 [1m--typedef-alias[22m no-typedef|add-typedef                      Add typedef alias to unions, structs, and enums (no        
                                                             typedef by default)                                        
 [1m--print-style[22m print-formatted|print-unformatted             Which cJSON print should be used (formatted by default)    
 [1m--type-style[22m pascal-case|underscore-case|camel-case|upper-  Naming style for types                                     
 underscore-case|pascal-case-upper-acronyms|camel-case-                                                                 
 upper-acronyms                                                                                                         
 [1m--member-style[22m pascal-case|underscore-case|camel-           Naming style for members                                   
 case|upper-underscore-case|pascal-case-upper-                                                                          
 acronyms|camel-case-upper-acronyms                                                                                     
 [1m--enumerator-style[22m pascal-case|underscore-case|camel-       Naming style for enumerators                               
 case|upper-underscore-case|pascal-case-upper-                                                                          
 acronyms|camel-case-upper-acronyms                                                                                     
 [1m--[no-]header-only[22m                                          Generate headers only (on by default)                      

[1mOptions for C++[22m

 [1m--source-style[22m single-source|multi-source                   Source code generation type,  whether to generate single   
                                                             or multiple source files                                   
 [1m--include-location[22m local-include|global-include             Whether json.hpp is to be located globally or locally      
 [1m--code-format[22m with-struct|with-getter-setter                Generate classes with getters/setters, instead of structs  
 [1m--wstring[22m use-string|use-wstring                            Store strings using Utf-16 std::wstring, rather than Utf-8 
                                                             std::string                                                
 [1m--const-style[22m west-const|east-const                         Put const to the left/west (const T) or right/east (T      
                                                             const)                                                     
 [1m--[no-]just-types[22m                                           Plain types only (off by default)                          
 [1m--namespace[22m NAME                                            Name of the generated namespace(s)                         
 [1m--enum-type[22m NAME                                            Type of enum class                                         
 [1m--type-style[22m pascal-case|original-case|underscore-          Naming style for types                                     
 case|camel-case|upper-underscore-case|pascal-case-upper-                                                               
 acronyms|camel-case-upper-acronyms                                                                                     
 [1m--member-style[22m pascal-case|original-case|underscore-        Naming style for members                                   
 case|camel-case|upper-underscore-case|pascal-case-upper-                                                               
 acronyms|camel-case-upper-acronyms                                                                                     
 [1m--enumerator-style[22m pascal-case|original-case|underscore-    Naming style for enumerators                               
 case|camel-case|upper-underscore-case|pascal-case-upper-                                                               
 acronyms|camel-case-upper-acronyms                                                                                     
 [1m--[no-]boost[22m                                                Require a dependency on boost. Without boost, C++17 is     
                                                             required (off by default)                                  
 [1m--[no-]hide-null-optional[22m                                   Hide null value for optional field (off by default)        

